        "system": {
          "actionType": {
            "value": "passive"
          },
          "actions": {
            "value": null
          },
          "category": "ancestry",
          "description": {
            "value": "<p>You have either trained a giant moray eel since its hatching or have tamed one in the wild. You gain the @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.feats-srd.Item.Bonded Animal] skill feat, even if you don't meet the prerequisites, to bond with a giant moray eel. When you @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.actionspf2e.Item.Command an Animal]{Command this Animal} while you are mounted on it to take a move action, you automatically succeed instead of needing to attempt a check.</p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>Special</strong> If you have the Elver Pet or Growing Eel Friend ancestry feats, you can choose to have that pet become your bonded animal. You don't need to spend 7 days of downtime to bond with the eel, and you automatically succeed at the Nature check. You can then retrain those feats.</p>"
          },
          "level": {
            "value": 9
          },
          "prerequisites": {
            "value": []
          },
